  "body": "### Description\r\n\r\nHello,\r\n\r\nIn the [official documentation](https://github.com/matrix-org/synapse/blob/56efa9b1672abcdf1f42bebcc3c7dd0b4fa40067/docs/admin_api/user_admin_api.md?plain=1#L360-L361), `erase : true` should delete `displayname` **BUT is not the case** \r\n\r\nI am still able to see the user display name when I query our room. \r\n\r\n<img width=\"514\" alt=\"Screenshot 2023-03-30 at 17 58 37\" src=\"https://user-images.githubusercontent.com/112070976/228895342-7b5100ff-8bfa-4d7c-8bfc-9fd0faa4c325.png\">\r\n\r\n\r\n### Steps to reproduce\r\n\r\n 1. Create a user with a `displayname`\r\n 1. Deactivate a user with `erase : true `\r\n 2. Query the room where the user was joined\r\n\r\n### Homeserver\r\n\r\nmy private server\r\n\r\n### Synapse Version\r\n\r\nsynapse version 1.79\r\n\r\n### Installation Method\r\n\r\nDebian packages from packages.matrix.org\r\n\r\n### Database\r\n\r\npostgres \r\n\r\n### Workers\r\n\r\nSingle process\r\n\r\n### Platform\r\n\r\nAll\r\n\r\n### Configuration\r\n\r\n_No response_\r\n\r\n### Relevant log output\r\n\r\n```shell\r\nPlease see the attached picture\r\n```\r\n\r\n\r\n### Anything else that would be useful to know?\r\n\r\n_No response_",
